Keira Kernel
============

Keira is a freestanding, multi-language x86_64 kernel. It
manages system hardware resources, coordinates low-level C drivers, and
provides a preemptive priority multitasking scheduler, 62 system calls,
AHCI SATA storage driver, NVMe PCIe Driver, VBE Framebuffer, USB Host Controller, LKM, HPET Timer, PCIe ECAM/MSI, io_uring Async I/O, NX/KASLR, Futex Threading, cgroups, EXT4 Driver, KVM Hypervisor, TPM 2.0, BPF Engine, DMA Allocator, Syslog Buffer, MAC Security, POSIX Timers, Pipe Splice, ACPI Power, PMU Counters, EventFD, Seccomp BPF, Swap Space, Epoll, Message Queues, POSIX Signals & Job Control, USB Mass Storage & HID Subsystem, Hardware RAID & LVM, POSIX Shared Memory IPC, Stateful Netfilter IPv4 Firewall Engine,
Native TLS 1.3 Cryptographic Engine, IPC Shared Memory & Pipe subsystems, Multi-User Accounts & Hostname, POSIX File Permissions & Multi-TTY, Userland Socket API, Native KCC Compiler (Keira C Compiler),
74 native shell commands, and a system shell controlled by a hyper-modular Rust kernel workspace.


Quick Start
-----------

* Get the latest code: https://github.com/mrvlous/keira
* Setup the workspace: See docs/contributing/setup.md
* Build & run the kernel: `make run`
* Automated test suite: `make test`

